## Dev lane — WSL Debian (never build on Windows)

Windows keeps cargo off PATH on purpose (VS Build Tools rejected; keeps the Doctor's day-one finding real — a stale off-PATH rustup toolchain exists in the user profile but plays no part). All development is in WSL Debian; the repo stays in exactly one place.

    # build + test
    wsl -d Debian -- bash -lc 'cd /mnt/c/Users/shuga/Desktop/shared/factory/GRAPHEINA && cargo test'

    # run the Doctor
    wsl -d Debian -- bash -lc 'cd /mnt/c/Users/shuga/Desktop/shared/factory/GRAPHEINA && ./target/debug/grapheina doctor'

    # the canonical simulation (23 checks, runs the real binary)
    wsl -d Debian -- bash -lc 'cd /mnt/c/Users/shuga/Desktop/shared/factory/GRAPHEINA && bash docs/features/scaffolding/simulate.sh'

    # the honest day-one finding (git visible, cargo hidden) -> ✗ cargo, exit 2
    wsl -d Debian -- bash -lc 'cd /mnt/c/Users/shuga/Desktop/shared/factory/GRAPHEINA && env PATH=/usr/bin:/bin ./target/debug/grapheina doctor && echo FINE || echo BROKEN'

Quirks: through `wsl.exe` from PowerShell, `$?` is mangled — read exit codes with `&& echo OK || echo BAD`. POSIX default-path fallback: PATH unset still finds `/usr/bin/git`; hermetic tests use `PATH=/nonexistent`.

